        {
          "id": "header_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Vegan Mushroom Risotto",
          "variant": "h2"
        },
        {
          "id": "meta_row",
          "component": "Row",
          "align": "center",
          "children": [
            "icon_vegan",
            "text_vegan",
            "icon_time",
            "text_time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "icon_vegan",
          "component": "Image",
          "url": "/assets/vegan_friendly_icon.png",
          "variant": "icon"
        },
        {
          "id": "text_vegan",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": " Vegan Friendly  "
        },
        {
          "id": "icon_time",
          "component": "Image",
          "url": "/assets/simple_icon_time.png",
          "variant": "icon"
        },
        {
          "id": "text_time",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": " ~40 mins"
        },
        {
          "id": "hero_image",
          "component": "Image",
          "url": "/assets/risotto_ai_funghi_porcini.jpg",
          "variant": "largeFeature"
        },
        {
          "id": "summary_text",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "This vegan mushroom risotto serves 4 and achieves a luxurious, creamy texture through the high starch content of arborio rice and the traditional 'mantecatura' finishing technique using high-quality olive oil rather than butter. The key is constant agitation to release starch and a vigorous stir at the end to emulsify the fats.",
          "variant": "body"
        },
        {
          "id": "divider_1",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "ingredients_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Ingredients",
          "variant": "h3"
        },
        {
          "id": "ingredients_list",
          "component": "List",
          "direction": "vertical",
          "children": [
            "ing_1",
            "ing_2",
            "ing_3",
            "ing_4",
            "ing_5",
            "ing_6",
            "ing_7",
            "ing_8",
            "ing_9",
            "ing_10",
            "ing_11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_1",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 1.5 cups Arborio rice (do not rinse)"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_2",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 1 lb (450g) Mixed mushrooms (cremini, shiitake, oyster), sliced"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_3",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 6 cups Vegetable broth, low sodium (keep simmering in a separate pot)"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_4",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 1 small Yellow onion, finely diced"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_5",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 2 cloves Garlic, minced"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_6",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 1/2 cup Dry white wine (Sauvignon Blanc or Pinot Grigio) or extra broth"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_7",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 4 tbsp Extra virgin olive oil, divided"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_8",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 2 tbsp Nutritional yeast (optional, adds savory 'cheesy' depth)"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_9",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• 1 tsp Fresh thyme leaves"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_10",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• Salt and black pepper to taste"
        },
        {
          "id": "ing_11",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "• Fresh parsley, chopped (for garnish)"
        },
        {
          "id": "divider_2",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "instructions_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Instructions",
          "variant": "h3"
        },
        {
          "id": "step_1_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "1. Sear the Mushrooms",
          "variant": "h4"
        },
        {
          "id": "step_1_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Heat 1 tbsp olive oil in a large, heavy-bottomed pot over medium-high heat. Add mushrooms and cook until browned and liquid has evaporated (about 5-8 minutes). Remove mushrooms from the pot and set aside."
        },
        {
          "id": "step_2_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "2. Toast the Rice",
          "variant": "h4"
        },
        {
          "id": "step_2_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Reduce heat to medium. Add 1 tbsp olive oil and the diced onion to the pot. Sauté until translucent (3-4 minutes). Add the arborio rice and toast, stirring constantly, for 1-2 minutes until the edges of the grains are translucent. Add garlic and thyme, cooking for another 30 seconds until fragrant."
        },
        {
          "id": "step_3_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "3. Deglaze",
          "variant": "h4"
        },
        {
          "id": "step_3_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Pour in the white wine. Stir constantly until the wine is fully absorbed by the rice."
        },
        {
          "id": "step_4_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "4. The Risotto Method",
          "variant": "h4"
        },
        {
          "id": "step_4_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Add the hot vegetable broth one ladle (approx. 1/2 cup) at a time. Stir frequently. Wait until the liquid is almost completely absorbed before adding the next ladle. This process should take 18-20 minutes. The constant stirring is crucial for releasing starch."
        },
        {
          "id": "step_5_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "5. Finish (The Creamy Step)",
          "variant": "h4"
        },
        {
          "id": "step_5_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Taste the rice; it should be tender but with a slight bite (al dente). If it is too hard, add a splash more broth.\n\nCrucial Step: Remove the pot from the heat. Stir in the cooked mushrooms, nutritional yeast, and the remaining 2 tbsp of olive oil. Stir vigorously for 30 seconds to emulsify the oil with the starchy liquid—this creates the creamy texture without dairy."
        },
        {
          "id": "step_6_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "6. Serve",
          "variant": "h4"
        },
        {
          "id": "step_6_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Season with salt and plenty of black pepper. Garnish with fresh parsley and serve immediately."
        },
        {
          "id": "divider_3",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "secrets_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Secrets to Dairy-Free Creaminess",
          "variant": "h3"
        },
        {
          "id": "rice_image",
          "component": "Image",
          "url": "/assets/arborio_rice.jpg",
          "variant": "mediumFeature"
        },
        {
          "id": "secrets_table",
          "component": "List",
          "direction": "vertical",
          "children": [
            "sec_row_header",
            "sec_row_1",
